#     take 16-bit ids (ShootType_t is uint16_t); Game.setMissileEffect (0045) takes 16-bit ids on both sides; monsters.xml shootEffect
#     and items.xml shootType also take a number (a missile with no name).
#   * Missile 254 stays CONST_ANI_WEAPONTYPE (resolved before anything is sent): new missiles start at 256.
# Nothing here sends an id above 255 by itself: data only does from client pair 83 (server/tools/client_pair.py PAIR_MISSILE_U16).
